{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25541",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Bytes is a utility library for working with bytes. From version 1.2.1  ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Bytes is a utility library for working with bytes. From version 1.2.1 to before 1.11.1, Bytes is vulnerable to integer overflow in BytesMut::reserve. In the unique reclaim path of BytesMut::reserve, if the condition \"v_capacity \u003e= new_cap + offset\" uses an unchecked addition. When new_cap + offset overflows usize in release builds, this condition may incorrectly pass, causing self.cap to be set to a value that exceeds the actual allocated capacity. Subsequent APIs such as spare_capacity_mut() then trust this corrupted cap value and may create out-of-bounds slices, leading to UB. This behavior is observable in release builds (integer overflow wraps), whereas debug builds panic due to overflow checks. This issue has been patched in version 1.11.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25541",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-25541\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: bytes\nFixed Version: 1.11.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-25541](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25541)\nBytes is a utility library for working with bytes. From version 1.2.1 to before 1.11.1, Bytes is vulnerable to integer overflow in BytesMut::reserve. In the unique reclaim path of BytesMut::reserve, if the condition \"v_capacity \u003e= new_cap + offset\" uses an unchecked addition. When new_cap + offset overflows usize in release builds, this condition may incorrectly pass, causing self.cap to be set to a value that exceeds the actual allocated capacity. Subsequent APIs such as spare_capacity_mut() then trust this corrupted cap value and may create out-of-bounds slices, leading to UB. This behavior is observable in release builds (integer overflow wraps), whereas debug builds panic due to overflow checks. This issue has been patched in version 1.11.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-25541**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|bytes|1.11.1|[CVE-2026-25541](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25541)|\n\nBytes is a utility library for working with bytes. From version 1.2.1 to before 1.11.1, Bytes is vulnerable to integer overflow in BytesMut::reserve. In the unique reclaim path of BytesMut::reserve, if the condition \"v_capacity \u003e= new_cap + offset\" uses an unchecked addition. When new_cap + offset overflows usize in release builds, this condition may incorrectly pass, causing self.cap to be set to a value that exceeds the actual allocated capacity. Subsequent APIs such as spare_capacity_mut() then trust this corrupted cap value and may create out-of-bounds slices, leading to UB. This behavior is observable in release builds (integer overflow wraps), whereas debug builds panic due to overflow checks. This issue has been patched in version 1.11.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "`IterMut` violates Stacked Borrows by invalidating internal pointer"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Affected versions of this crate contain a soundness issue in the `IterMut` iterator implementation. The `IterMut::next` and `IterMut::next_back` methods temporarily create an exclusive reference to the key when dereferencing the internal node pointer.\n\nThis invalidates the shared pointer held by the internal `HashMap`, violating Stacked Borrows rules."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: lru\nFixed Version: 0.16.3\nLink: [GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j)\nAffected versions of this crate contain a soundness issue in the `IterMut` iterator implementation. The `IterMut::next` and `IterMut::next_back` methods temporarily create an exclusive reference to the key when dereferencing the internal node pointer.\n\nThis invalidates the shared pointer held by the internal `HashMap`, violating Stacked Borrows rules.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|lru|0.16.3|[GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j)|\n\nAffected versions of this crate contain a soundness issue in the `IterMut` iterator implementation. The `IterMut::next` and `IterMut::next_back` methods temporarily create an exclusive reference to the key when dereferencing the internal node pointer.\n\nThis invalidates the shared pointer held by the internal `HashMap`, violating Stacked Borrows rules."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.7,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41676",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming langua ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.27 to before 0.10.78, Deriver::derive (and PkeyCtxRef::derive) sets len = buf.len() and passes it as the in/out length to EVP_PKEY_derive, relying on OpenSSL to honor it. On OpenSSL 1.1.x, X25519, X448, DH and HKDF-extract ignore the incoming *keylen, unconditionally writing the full shared secret (32/56/prime-size bytes). A caller passing a short slice gets a heap/stack overflow from safe code. OpenSSL 3.x providers do check, so this only impacts older OpenSSL. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41676",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41676\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.78\nLink: [CVE-2026-41676](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41676)\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.27 to before 0.10.78, Deriver::derive (and PkeyCtxRef::derive) sets len = buf.len() and passes it as the in/out length to EVP_PKEY_derive, relying on OpenSSL to honor it. On OpenSSL 1.1.x, X25519, X448, DH and HKDF-extract ignore the incoming *keylen, unconditionally writing the full shared secret (32/56/prime-size bytes). A caller passing a short slice gets a heap/stack overflow from safe code. OpenSSL 3.x providers do check, so this only impacts older OpenSSL. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41676**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|openssl|0.10.78|[CVE-2026-41676](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41676)|\n\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.27 to before 0.10.78, Deriver::derive (and PkeyCtxRef::derive) sets len = buf.len() and passes it as the in/out length to EVP_PKEY_derive, relying on OpenSSL to honor it. On OpenSSL 1.1.x, X25519, X448, DH and HKDF-extract ignore the incoming *keylen, unconditionally writing the full shared secret (32/56/prime-size bytes). A caller passing a short slice gets a heap/stack overflow from safe code. OpenSSL 3.x providers do check, so this only impacts older OpenSSL. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 7.2,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41678",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming langua ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From  to before 0.10.78, aes::unwrap_key() contains an incorrect assertion: it checks that out.len() + 8 \u003c= in_.len(), but this condition is reversed. The intended invariant is out.len() \u003e= in_.len() - 8, ensuring the output buffer is large enough. Because of the inverted check, the function only accepts buffers at or below the minimum required size and rejects larger ones. If a smaller buffer is provided the function will write past the end of out by in_.len() - 8 - out.len() bytes, causing an out-of-bounds write from a safe public function. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41678",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41678\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.78\nLink: [CVE-2026-41678](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41678)\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From  to before 0.10.78, aes::unwrap_key() contains an incorrect assertion: it checks that out.len() + 8 \u003c= in_.len(), but this condition is reversed. The intended invariant is out.len() \u003e= in_.len() - 8, ensuring the output buffer is large enough. Because of the inverted check, the function only accepts buffers at or below the minimum required size and rejects larger ones. If a smaller buffer is provided the function will write past the end of out by in_.len() - 8 - out.len() bytes, causing an out-of-bounds write from a safe public function. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41678**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|openssl|0.10.78|[CVE-2026-41678](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41678)|\n\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From  to before 0.10.78, aes::unwrap_key() contains an incorrect assertion: it checks that out.len() + 8 \u003c= in_.len(), but this condition is reversed. The intended invariant is out.len() \u003e= in_.len() - 8, ensuring the output buffer is large enough. Because of the inverted check, the function only accepts buffers at or below the minimum required size and rejects larger ones. If a smaller buffer is provided the function will write past the end of out by in_.len() - 8 - out.len() bytes, causing an out-of-bounds write from a safe public function. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 7.2,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41681",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming langua ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.10.39 to before 0.10.78, EVP_DigestFinal() always writes EVP_MD_CTX_size(ctx) to the out buffer. If out is smaller than that, MdCtxRef::digest_final() writes past its end, usually corrupting the stack. This is reachable from safe Rust. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41681",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41681\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.78\nLink: [CVE-2026-41681](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41681)\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.10.39 to before 0.10.78, EVP_DigestFinal() always writes EVP_MD_CTX_size(ctx) to the out buffer. If out is smaller than that, MdCtxRef::digest_final() writes past its end, usually corrupting the stack. This is reachable from safe Rust. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41681**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|openssl|0.10.78|[CVE-2026-41681](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41681)|\n\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.10.39 to before 0.10.78, EVP_DigestFinal() always writes EVP_MD_CTX_size(ctx) to the out buffer. If out is smaller than that, MdCtxRef::digest_final() writes past its end, usually corrupting the stack. This is reachable from safe Rust. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 8.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41898",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming langua ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.24 to before 0.10.78, the FFI trampolines behind SslContextBuilder::set_psk_client_callback, set_psk_server_callback, set_cookie_generate_cb, and set_stateless_cookie_generate_cb forwarded the user closure's returned usize directly to OpenSSL without checking it against the \u0026mut [u8] that was handed to the closure. This can lead to buffer overflows and other unintended consequences. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41898",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41898\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.78\nLink: [CVE-2026-41898](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41898)\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.24 to before 0.10.78, the FFI trampolines behind SslContextBuilder::set_psk_client_callback, set_psk_server_callback, set_cookie_generate_cb, and set_stateless_cookie_generate_cb forwarded the user closure's returned usize directly to OpenSSL without checking it against the \u0026mut [u8] that was handed to the closure. This can lead to buffer overflows and other unintended consequences. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41898**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|openssl|0.10.78|[CVE-2026-41898](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41898)|\n\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.24 to before 0.10.78, the FFI trampolines behind SslContextBuilder::set_psk_client_callback, set_psk_server_callback, set_cookie_generate_cb, and set_stateless_cookie_generate_cb forwarded the user closure's returned usize directly to OpenSSL without checking it against the \u0026mut [u8] that was handed to the closure. This can lead to buffer overflows and other unintended consequences. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 8.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-44662",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming langua ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language. From 0.10.0 to before 0.10.79, CipherCtxRef::cipher_update, CipherCtxRef::cipher_update_vec, and symm::Crypter::update incorrectly sized output buffers when used with AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers (EVP_aes_{128,192,256}_wrap_pad). For a non-multiple-of-8 input, OpenSSL writes up to 7 bytes past the end of the caller's buffer or Vec, producing attacker-controllable heap corruption when the plaintext length is attacker-influenced. This only impacts users using AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.79."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44662",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-44662\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.79\nLink: [CVE-2026-44662](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44662)\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language. From 0.10.0 to before 0.10.79, CipherCtxRef::cipher_update, CipherCtxRef::cipher_update_vec, and symm::Crypter::update incorrectly sized output buffers when used with AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers (EVP_aes_{128,192,256}_wrap_pad). For a non-multiple-of-8 input, OpenSSL writes up to 7 bytes past the end of the caller's buffer or Vec, producing attacker-controllable heap corruption when the plaintext length is attacker-influenced. This only impacts users using AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.79.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-44662**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|openssl|0.10.79|[CVE-2026-44662](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44662)|\n\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language. From 0.10.0 to before 0.10.79, CipherCtxRef::cipher_update, CipherCtxRef::cipher_update_vec, and symm::Crypter::update incorrectly sized output buffers when used with AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers (EVP_aes_{128,192,256}_wrap_pad). For a non-multiple-of-8 input, OpenSSL writes up to 7 bytes past the end of the caller's buffer or Vec, producing attacker-controllable heap corruption when the plaintext length is attacker-influenced. This only impacts users using AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.79."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 5.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-45784",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl: Potential out-of-bounds write in `CipherCtxRef::cipher_update_inplace` for AES-KW-PAD ciphers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`CipherCtxRef::cipher_update_inplace` incorrectly sized output buffers when used with AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers (EVP_aes_{128,192,256}_wrap_pad). For a non-multiple-of-8 input, OpenSSL writes up to 7 bytes past the end of the caller's buffer or Vec, producing attacker-controllable heap corruption when the plaintext length is attacker-influenced.\n\nThis only impacts users using AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers.\n\nThis method was missed in the fix for GHSA-xv59-967r-8726"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45784",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-45784\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.80\nLink: [CVE-2026-45784](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45784)\n`CipherCtxRef::cipher_update_inplace` incorrectly sized output buffers when used with AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers (EVP_aes_{128,192,256}_wrap_pad). For a non-multiple-of-8 input, OpenSSL writes up to 7 bytes past the end of the caller's buffer or Vec, producing attacker-controllable heap corruption when the plaintext length is attacker-influenced.\n\nThis only impacts users using AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers.\n\nThis method was missed in the fix for GHSA-xv59-967r-8726",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-45784**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|openssl|0.10.80|[CVE-2026-45784](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45784)|\n\n`CipherCtxRef::cipher_update_inplace` incorrectly sized output buffers when used with AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers (EVP_aes_{128,192,256}_wrap_pad). For a non-multiple-of-8 input, OpenSSL writes up to 7 bytes past the end of the caller's buffer or Vec, producing attacker-controllable heap corruption when the plaintext length is attacker-influenced.\n\nThis only impacts users using AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers.\n\nThis method was missed in the fix for GHSA-xv59-967r-8726"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 5.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
